{
  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a sustained uptrend (e.g., >72 EUR) followed by a flat or slightly declining sentiment score, the model consistently overestimates future prices by 5-10% and fails to anticipate immediate mean reversion.",
    "The model exhibits significant lag in detecting volatility spikes; when true outcomes drop sharply after a high (e.g., from 73+ to <65), the forecast remains anchored near the previous average for weeks.",
    "Negative sentiment signals (-0.25) appearing late in the history window are ignored by the model, which continues projecting linear growth despite clear downward pressure indicators.",
    "In high-volatility regimes (standard deviation > 3 EUR/day), the model's forecast horizon is too long and smooth, failing to capture the 'V-shaped' recovery patterns seen in true outcomes after deep corrections.",
    "Apply a dynamic correction factor: subtract 5-8% from the model's 30-day projection when the last 5 days of history show a price decline >10% and sentiment is neutral or negative."
  ]
}
